<title>JORDAN: Jordan August trade deficit widens 15 pct vs July.</title>
<headline>Jordan August trade deficit widens 15 pct vs July.</headline>
<dateline>AMMAN 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jordan's August trade deficit widened by 15 percent to 153.4 million dinars ($216.7 million) from 133.5 million in July, hit by a rise in imports, the Central Bank bulletin said.</p>
<p>A rise in exports of construction materials and intermediate goods in August was wiped out by a slump in sales of crude materials and consumer goods, the bank said.</p>
<p>Imports of almost all goods rose in August to a total of 269.7 million dinars, five percent up on July's 256.3 million. The August 1996 imports were also 25 percent up on the same period last year.</p>
<p>(All figures in millions of dinars)</p>
<p>			   Aug 96   July 96   Aug 95     1995    1994</p>
<p>Domestic exports	96.25    103.19    91.88    1,004     794</p>
<p>Re-Exports		20.03     19.59    17.42	237     201</p>
<p>Imports		  269.70    256.28   215.20    2,590   2,363</p>
<p>Trade Balance	 -153.42   -133.50  -105.90   -1,349  -1,368</p>
<p>$1 = 0.7080 dinars</p>
<p>-- Amman newsroom 9626 623 776</p>
